    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0547" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg473"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/8265</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-15T19:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.21 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1767. Von der Heydt, attached to the German Legation here,
                    is endeavoring through a neutral to send me a written statement for <pb
                        facs="0548" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/> transmission to you.
                        Heydt is said to be an intimate of Kühlmann and to be his special man in the
                    German Legation here. He sends word through the neutral that the statement is in
                    connection with the German desire to have a preliminary and confidential
                    decision of a possible basis for peace. Do you wish me to receive this
                    statement? I respectfully request your answer by Monday morning if possible so
                    that the fact that I have cabled you may not be apparent as that would make the
                    matter undesirably official on our part.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
